WEBVTT

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:14.950
I raced with pride on the line.
Coward! You call yourself a racer?!

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.950
Though sadly defeated, I decided to
join the Trans-America race!

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:24.450
The start is near! Appare!
We're rivals from here on out!

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.830
Hey! Coffee, please!

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.040
With pleasure!

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:33.830
--Here
--Thanks.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:34.910
Here.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.950
Kosame!

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.660
That's enough. Go home.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.870
Got it!

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.580
Thanks for everything.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.500
Huh? Oh, was today your last day?

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.500
Yes. The race starts tomorrow.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.950
Here's a parting gift.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.200
Really?

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.700
Thank you.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.120
Come back whenever you want.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.000
I appreciate it.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.330
However, once I win the prize money,
I'll return to my country!

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.160
Just don't die.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.250
Right!

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:22.290
"Episode 5: The Eve, and..."

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.120
Hey, Appare. It's time to go.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.660
Good grief.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.370
What are you doing?

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.290
Going to the pre-race party.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.080
He can work without sleeping for days,

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:51.790
but then he crashes and sleeps like a log.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:55.830
Once he's out, nothing will wake him up.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.370
Hey, Hototo. Get ready to go.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:01:59.830
Huh? Me?

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:02.700
Obviously. You're racing with us.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.660
You're letting me join the race?

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.580
Huh? Didn't you hear from Appare?

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.080
Hear what?

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:16.000
Good grief! I was against bringing
a kid on a dangerous race,

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.450
but Appare said you'd make a good guide.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:20.540
A guide...

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:24.040
You know the land, you can
read the weather and stars,

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:28.000
and you know how to get
food and water in the wild, right?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.620
That's pretty impressive... for a child.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.500
Don't treat me like a child.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.450
He even said he'd tell you himself...

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.950
Well? You don't have to.
It'll be dangerous and--

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.870
I'll go. I'm in debt to Appare.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.950
Great. Party it is.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:49.080
I'll go to the race,
but not the party. I hate crowds.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:53.910
Don't be so selfish. All the racers
were told to come. Besides...

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:56.750
We get a free meal out of it.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.370
Will that guy be there?

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:03.540
That guy? Oh, you mean Dylan or something?

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.410
Yeah, I imagine.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.250
Then I'll go.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.450
You better be a good boy.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.950
I just wanna ask him something.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:26.290
For the prize money, you're only
getting 20% since you're just a kid.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:30.410
Appare's our mechanic and
I'm our guide. What are you?

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:33.870
I'm... our leader!

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:40.500
Is this the place? The feast
might be better than I thought!

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:46.330
How does he even sleep like this?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.500
Think he's faking it?

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:51.410
Appare! Kosame! Hototo!

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.500
Huh?

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.120
Wha--?! Xialian!

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.870
Um, is he okay?!

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:04.500
Yeah, he's fine! You just look
so different, it surprised me.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.500
Is it weird?

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:09.250
No, it's pretty.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:13.370
Right? The team got me this as a present.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:18.370
After all, this is my introduction
as a racer to the world.

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:19.910
Where am I?

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:24.580
Finally up? Like I thought,
you're doomed without a leader!

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:25.950
Appare.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:28.750
Thanks.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.290
Yeah.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.500
--Welcome.
--Here.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.410
Shall we go inside?

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.580
Sure.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:40.290
So it wasn't just racers invited to the party?

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:42.330
It's a big event.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:45.950
There's B.I.G. BOSS VIPs, team sponsors,

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:48.910
the paper, and politicians here, too.

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:50.290
Yeah?

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.120
Welcome.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.580
Thanks. Let's head inside.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:58.830
Let's eat and get outta here.
I've got places to be.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:02.370
Because your car isn't done.
Don't try to sound cool.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.330
Huh? Still?

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.040
--Wait.
--Hmm?

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.950
You can't enter like that.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:07.830
Huh?

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:10.080
The party has a dress code.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.500
A dress code?

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.040
Didn't you read the invitation?

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.620
Of course not.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:16.870
You are...?

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:21.540
I'm Seth Rich Carter,
someone in charge of this race.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:24.750
You can't enter without formal attire.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:30.700
Your outfit is appropriate,
but the rest of you three...

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:35.250
Hideous. You look like monkeys
that escaped from a circus.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:38.000
This <i>is </i>my formal attire.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.500
This is why I hate crowds.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:46.160
They're racers. They have a right
to draw for starting position.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:50.290
They should start at the end
so as to not hinder the race.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:51.290
Hinder?

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:55.160
I read the paper. They say
you made your own car?

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.450
That's right.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.370
Know your place, bumpkins.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.200
Tsk! Appare, say something!

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.410
If we can't eat, I'm leaving.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:07.750
Not that! You've gotta say something cooler!

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.620
Hey! Someone corral these monkeys!

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:11.450
Monkeys?

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:15.200
You guys don't belong in a place like this.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.160
Crazy TJ...

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.910
That's one of the Thousand Three...

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.700
Thousand Three?

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.540
Outlaws a match for a thousand men.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:43.410
They were once seven men
named the Thousand Seven.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:47.160
But now it's said only three remain.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:52.700
Is this where the party's at?

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:53.620
Yeah...

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:58.580
Heard there's a dress code.
Well? Is this good enough?

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:02.120
O-Of course. Please head right in.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.200
Thought as much.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:07.750
--Take care of this.
--Sure!

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:11.040
Hey! If he's okay, I am, too!

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.910
--Whoa!
--Appare!

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.290
Huh? Who the hell are you?

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:17.160
Likewise.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:24.790
You've got some cool hair there.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:29.160
Hair? Yours looks like you blew something up.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.500
Hey! Don't be rude!

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:35.540
You're funny! I like you!

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:37.200
Come drink with me!

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.160
No way, I don't drink. Don't touch me!

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:42.500
It's fine if we go in, right?

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:45.410
At the very least, wear a tie!

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:55.250
Bored?

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:59.370
Huh? Yeah... I'm bad at formal stuff.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.660
Should we leave?

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.540
Huh?

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.790
I can't exactly do that.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:08.450
If I'm gonna succeed my dad,
I've gotta get used to it.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:09.620
That's true.

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:12.700
Huh? Mr. Carter!

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:16.000
Mr. Lyon! Welcome to the party!

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.750
Please, feel free to call me Seth.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:21.580
Did something happen?

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:24.160
Well, it's embarrassing...

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:28.370
It appears there's some riffraff
among the racers, so make sure--

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:30.080
Al! Sofia!

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:32.250
Hey, Kosame!

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:35.040
Hello there, Sofia!

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.910
Hello! That's a lovely necktie!

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:40.120
Yup. It's formal attire!

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.450
Where's Appare?

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.250
Over there.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.910
You know him?

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:47.290
Yes. He's my rival.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:48.830
Rival?!

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:51.830
Appare! You finished your car, right?

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:54.160
My goodness...

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:56.700
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:08:56.700 --> 00:09:00.160
Welcome to the pre-race celebration!

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:05.540
As the name suggests,
whoever crosses America the fastest wins!

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:08.120
All vehicles are allowed!

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:12.910
It starts here in LA and ends
in New York on the east coast!

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.660
The total prize pool is...!

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.790
$1,510,000!

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:23.000
The rules are simple--you can't
change vehicles on the way.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.200
You may not use the railroad.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:28.200
Also, once you enter a supply point,

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:32.080
you must stay in the city
for at least eight hours.

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:36.950
Teams can decide whether or not
to use the supply points.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:40.910
It's faster if we don't, right?

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.950
You can't reach the finish without 'em.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:47.000
There's only a few cities with gas.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:51.370
If you avoid supply points,
you end up going even further.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:54.000
But isn't ours steam powered?

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.330
For now, yeah.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:56.290
For now?

00:09:56.290 --> 00:10:02.700
This race was organized to show
the appeal of gasoline cars, after all.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:07.040
--Now then, let's introduce
the B.I.G BOSS sponsors of the race!
--Making gas available on the shortest route
is hugely beneficial for them.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.160
--B.I.G comes from the first letters of BNW,
Iron Motor Company, and Great Motors!
--Making gas available on the shortest route
is hugely beneficial for them.

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:12.580
--B.I.G comes from the first letters of BNW,
Iron Motor Company, and Great Motors!
--Besides, having to stop
eight hours to resupply

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:14.250
--B.I.G comes from the first letters of BNW,
Iron Motor Company, and Great Motors!
--benefits the B.I.G. BOSS teams
with their advantage in driving range.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:18.370
--These three auto giants joined forces
for this special event!
--benefits the B.I.G. BOSS teams
with their advantage in driving range.

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:23.200
--A survival race like never before!
The Trans-America Wild Race!
--Stopping lets them put their money
and manpower into fixing the car.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:24.450
--A survival race like never before!
The Trans-America Wild Race!
--The small teams are simply forced to wait.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:27.370
--Now, a word from the race's chief organizer--
--The small teams are simply forced to wait.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:27.870
--Now, a word from the race's chief organizer--
--It's unfair.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:28.500
--Great Motors' young CTO and
vice president of PR, Seth Rich Carter!
--It's unfair.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:35.620
--Great Motors' young CTO and
vice president of PR, Seth Rich Carter!
--Perhaps, but you'd never finish
this harsh of a race without supply points.

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:37.370
Welcome, everyone!

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:40.910
GM is proud to sponsor the Trans-America--

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:46.120
Whoa! My, my! Everyone's here!

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:52.000
I heard you're supposed to come late
to parties, but I guess I was wrong!

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.830
This is Gil of the Thousand Three!

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:57.910
I'm his partner, Chase!

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:02.160
That's... Gil the Butcher...!

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:07.660
No photos!

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:10.950
That's...

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:21.660
Well then, let's introduce
the teams and the racers!

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:26.910
Car number 1! Driving the fastest,
mightiest, Great Motors G1

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:32.450
is the race's top contender, Dylan G. Oldin!

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:34.870
Next is car number 777!

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:39.660
A car with pizzazz that's the pride of
Iron Motor Company, Crazy Z!

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:43.540
And its driver is... TJ!

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:50.000
Car number 9! Behind the wheel of
the speedy and snazzy BNW AL9

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:54.620
is the young scion from Europe, Al Lyon!

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:57.830
Car number 44!

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:02.540
This machine of his making, Tlaloc,
is a fortress on wheels!

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:06.200
Driving it... Gil T. Cigar!

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:07.330
Car number 86!

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:08.950
"Phoenix Lotus"
Car number 86!

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:11.370
"Phoenix Lotus"
Converted from a race car,

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:13.750
"Phoenix Lotus"
the Phoenix Lotus is driven by
the only woman driver, Jing Xialian!

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:16.540
the Phoenix Lotus is driven by
the only woman driver, Jing Xialian!

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:18.200
Car number 35!

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:23.040
Hoping to turn his life around
by winning a fortune in his GT3

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:25.250
is Richard Reaseman!

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:41.200
It won't be long, Claudia...

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:42.290
Hey.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.660
You know this tattoo, right?

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:52.000
Yeah, I remember you. You're relentless.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.790
A man with this tattoo
on his neck killed my dad

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.290
and took everything from my family.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.580
I'm taking it back.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:04.330
Not everything. You still have your life.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:07.870
Go home and love the family you've still got.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.660
And what would you do?

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:10.700
Huh?

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:14.450
If something precious was
taken from you, could you forget it?

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:23.410
Gil the Snake.

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:27.620
That's a famous tattoo among outlaws.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:29.370
It's Gil's trademark.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.450
Gil! It's him?!

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:36.290
Let go!

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:40.870
Good grief. I'm not done talking yet.

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:45.830
Gil's henchmen who swear
loyalty to him have that tattoo.

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:49.540
The guy you're after is probably one of them.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:53.580
During the race, he'll probably
meet with his henchmen.

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:58.410
If you truly want to get revenge,
hold your horses and wait.

00:13:58.410 --> 00:14:01.500
If you wanna die, that's easy enough.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:03.250
Suit yourself.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:08.160
How many henchmen does he have?

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:11.450
I don't know much about Gil myself.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.790
I doubt anyone really does.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:19.370
Except that he's a brutal savage who
shows no mercy to women or children.

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:26.910
Shit.

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:32.830
Finally, the last machine is car number 0!

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:38.000
Their car unfinished, this ninja and
samurai escort came from the East!

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:39.040
Ninja?

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:40.160
Escort?

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.080
Appare! Kosome! Hototo!

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:43.830
It's Kosame!

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:50.790
And now we'll begin the starting grid raffle
for tomorrow's race!

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:53.660
--The first day's pre-race
will award $10,000 to the--

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:54.830
--How pathetic!
--The first day's pre-race
will award $10,000 to the--

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:56.830
--Huh?
--You're gonna make me cry!

00:14:56.830 --> 00:15:01.500
A raffle?! Who do you
think we are, Girl Scouts?!

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.330
The best get the best position.

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:09.500
Got a problem with that?!

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:16.620
Hototo, eat while you still can.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:19.040
That's Crazy TJ for you.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:22.000
Mr. Oldin! Please, stop him!

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:22.830
Huh?

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:25.040
You're acquaintances, right?

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.580
But I like his idea.

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:28.410
Huh?

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:34.250
Let's get crazy! How 'bout
a tournament for pole position?!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:37.790
Hey, Appare?

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:40.700
I wat poe poshishon!

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:41.870
Huh?

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:44.290
As usual, you're making a scene.

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:49.200
Yo! It's been a while, Dylan.
Still being a closet pervert?

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.410
Staring at photos of women and--

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:53.160
You're dead.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:59.700
Yeah, man! Let's pick up where we left off?

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:00.950
Wait!

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:02.370
What?

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:05.120
I want pole position, too.

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:09.660
Aren't you the big mouth who said
you'd be driving in front of me?

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:14.290
By the honor and pride of the Lyon name,
I give way to no one!

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:15.750
Me, too!

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:18.620
Good grief. Screw it, I guess.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:24.500
I thought this race would be boring as hell,
but you people seem fun!

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.160
I ain't losing to a woman!

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:27.160
I'm going, too!

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:28.750
--Me, too!
--And me!

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.330
Me, too!

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:32.870
Damn these brats.

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:35.580
Gil, just wait right there.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:40.290
Mr. Oldin! It's too dangerous!
The race starts tomorrow!

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:44.870
If anyone ends up dying,
they wouldn't have lasted long anyhow.

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:45.790
Wha--?!

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:48.200
I'm settling the score with this guy.

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:51.620
Once I'm done, I'll take the rest of you on!

00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:54.160
Until then, compete among yourselves!

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:56.870
Let's party!

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:19.700
Ready? Go!

00:17:24.330 --> 00:17:29.040
A woman, huh? C'mon,
I'll even give you the first blow.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:49.910
Done!

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:51.910
Wha--?! Damn!

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:54.700
Please make this stop!

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:57.040
Hey! No photos!

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:59.200
I did it, Appare!

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:01.910
Huh? Where'd he go?

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:03.330
Back home.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:06.790
Huh? What about pole position?

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:28.660
Father... Fumi...

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:31.870
I'm winning this race and coming back home.

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:38.200
I wanna make it light.
Bring as little as you can.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:39.160
And food?

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:44.580
Don't need it. The first supply point
is just under 150 kilometers.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:47.790
Today's pre-race is all about speed.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:49.700
Where's your luggage?

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.290
Pack this.

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:55.250
That's it?

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:57.500
Tools are all I need.

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:14.790
It's finally complete?

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:17.160
No, not yet.

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:19.200
It won't be complete.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:21.620
It'll keep evolving.

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:23.370
Evolving?

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:35.660
All right, the Trans-America
Wild Race is about to start!

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:37.000
The rules are simple--

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:40.250
you drive your car from here
in Los Angeles across the country,

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:44.540
and the one who is the fastest
to arrive in New York is the winner!

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:49.120
The first day is a pre-race,
with a prize of $10,000 on the line!

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:53.700
The daredevil challengers competing
in this unprecedented survival race

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:58.160
are impatiently waiting for
the start signal to be given!

00:19:58.160 --> 00:20:02.040
Aren't you ready yet, Appare?!
The race is about to start! What are you doing?!

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:05.910
Final tuning. I'm hurrying. Keep quiet.

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:09.410
Sheesh, we're the only ones doing it.

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:12.330
Kosame, settle down. We have far to go.

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:14.410
You're a child; you be quiet.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:28.500
Appare, I'm going on ahead!

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:35.120
You've known for a long time that
today was the start of the race, right?

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:37.620
Why didn't you have this finished yesterday?!

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:39.080
--Done.
--Oh, good.

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:40.700
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:41.660
Hototo...

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:42.830
Right.

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:47.200
Hitch up your loincloth, Kosame.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:50.540
Huh? D-Drive safely...

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:56.330
So, let's go and see where this road leads!

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:59.250
Here we go!

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:02.450
Whoa!

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:07.950
Be careful, everyone.

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:35.250
There you are, Appare. Race me!

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:37.080
I'm not going to hold back!

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:39.450
Hmph, interesting guy.

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:44.500
Kosame, Hototo, hang on! We're gonna
blast out of here as fast as we can go!

00:21:55.450 --> 00:21:57.000
Pardon me.

00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:06.370
Wasn't that a little hectic?

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:12.410
No worries. As long as we leave it to him...

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:17.500
...this race will end in tragedy.

00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:47.410
"Next time"

00:23:47.410 --> 00:23:49.870
"Episode 6: I am Gil!"
